Profit Coach for Yorkshire MDs in groundworks, civils and allied trades | 43 years in business | Ranked World No.1 four years running | Take the 3-min BOSS Scorecard to see where your margin is going
```

### About

**About section**

```text
Be honest.

You've got a decent business. The turnover's there, the work's there, the lads are there.

But if you sat down tonight and worked out what the business actually pays you per hour for the risk and graft you carry, would the number feel right?

Most of the MDs I work with know something isn't quite right. They just don't know which bit to fix first. Or if they've got time to fix anything.

Behind the scenes it usually looks like this:

⭐ Margin that looked fine when you priced the job but had nowt in it by the time you finished
⭐ A contracts manager you hired to take pressure off but you're still doing half his job because it's quicker
⭐ Cash tight at month-end despite good turnover, and you can't explain where it went
⭐ Tenders sitting unpriced on your desk because you've been sorting a plant breakdown instead

That's not just how construction works. That's a fixable problem.

WHAT MOST MDs ACTUALLY WANT

Jobs that land the margin they priced. A team that sorts problems itself and stops ringing you for every decision. Cash that flows predictably. And a proper weekend where the phone stays quiet and nothing falls apart.

When those things work properly, the business starts paying you back for what you've put into it.

WHO THIS IS FOR

