_Personalise the opening line with something specific you noticed on their profile or company page: a project mentioned, a recent hire, a milestone posted. Do not send this without a real observation in the first line._

> **Who goes on the top 100 list:** An MD goes on the VIP list if three or more of these are true: groundworks, civils, drainage or allied trades; Yorkshire-based or within 40 miles of Leeds or Sheffield; turnover signals of £1.5M to £8M (team size, project mentions, fleet visible on profile); 10 or more years in business; active on LinkedIn in the last 90 days; no existing coach visible on their profile. Add anyone who has previously engaged with your content, replied to a message, or been referred by someone you trust. Review the list every quarter and remove anyone who has gone cold for more than 12 months.

### Nurture rhythm

- **Week 2:** Share something useful. Send a short observation or a post you have written that is relevant to their world. Something about margin, pricing, or team. No ask. No link to a call. Just something worth reading. One or two sentences of context, then the content.
- **Week 5:** BOSS Scorecard drop. Send the scorecard link with a single line of context. 'I have been sending this to a few MDs in the trade lately. Takes three minutes and usually throws up something worth knowing. Here is the link if you want it: {assessment_url}.' No pressure. No follow-up question.
- **Week 8:** Relevant trigger or insight. Share something tied to a real event: end of financial year, a busy tendering period, the summer squeeze on cash. Keep it to two or three sentences. Make it feel like something you noticed, not something you scheduled. End with one low-pressure question: 'Is this time of year usually a good one for you or does the cash get tight?'
- **Day 90:** Check-in. Send a plain, short message. 'Hi {first_name}, just checking in. It has been a few months since we last spoke. How is the business going at the moment? Any of the stuff we touched on still on your radar?' Nothing more. If they reply, restart the conversation from scratch. If they do not, move to a quarterly touch and keep them on the VIP list.

