| 7 | The question I ask every MD before we start. | Before any coaching work begins, Pam asks one question: where do you think the profit is going? The answer tells her everything about where to look first. This issue walks through the five most common answers she hears from MDs in the trade, and what is usually hiding behind each one. |

===== ninety:quarter (42s, 4943 chars)
One objective for the next 90 days: sign your first six clients onto The P.R.O.F.I.T. Programme and build the weekly rhythm that keeps the pipeline full after that.

- **£8,700/mo** Income target at six clients on £1,450 a month
- **6** Clients needed to hit that target
- **18 to 24** Value sessions needed to sign six clients (assume 25 to 33% conversion)
- **150 to 200** Real conversations needed to book that many calls

> **On the numbers:** These figures use your entry price of £1,450 a month and a six-client target. If you open with a six-month retainer at £7,800, the call and conversation numbers drop. Adjust as your first few calls give you a real conversion rate to work from.

### Week by week

- **Weeks 1 to 2:** Foundations locked. LinkedIn profile live and reflecting your construction specialism. BOSS Scorecard link active and tested. Value session named and calendar connected. Prospect list of 150 MDs in groundworks, civils, drainage and allied trades across Yorkshire built and ready. Your outreach message drafted and reviewed. Nothing goes out until the destination is working.
- **Weeks 2 to 4:** First campaign live. Start sending 20 connection requests a day to Steve-profile MDs in your target area. Handle replies daily, same day where possible. Goal by end of week four: 60 to 80 connections accepted, 15 to 20 real conversations started, two to four value sessions booked. First BOSS Scorecard completions coming in.
- **Weeks 4 to 8:** Calls every week, first client signed. Run at least two value sessions a week. Focus the session on the owner's numbers, not a presentation. Use the BOSS Scorecard to show exactly where margin is being capped before you suggest anything. Aim to sign your first client by week six and your second by week eight. Start posting on LinkedIn once a week: short, plain-spoken, grounded in a real problem Steve would recognise.
- **Weeks 8 to 12:** Second angle tested, referrals asked for. Test a second outreach angle, either a different entry line or a different trigger (cash-tight month, missed tender, site incident). Ask your first one or two clients who else in the trade they respect and whether they would make an introduction. Send your first short newsletter to the list you have been building. Review your price after three or four clients signed: if conversion is above 40%, the price is probably too low.

### Weekly numbers

| Activity | Per week |
| --- | --- |
| Connection requests sent to target MDs | 100 |
| New connections accepted (target rate: 30 to 40%) | 30 to 40 |
| Follow-up messages sent to accepted connections | All of them, within 48 hours |
| Real two-way conversations active | 10 to 15 |
| Value sessions booked | 2 to 4 |
| Value sessions run | 2 to 4 |
| Proposals or next steps offered | Equal to sessions run |
| New clients signed | 1 to 2 (from week six onward) |
| LinkedIn posts published | 1 |
| BOSS Scorecard completions followed up | Same day, every one |

### This week

1. **Get the destination ready before the first message goes out.** Check your LinkedIn profile reflects your construction specialism exactly as written in your positioning. Test the BOSS Scorecard link end to end: click it, complete it, confirm the result page works and that you get the notification. Connect your calendar to the value session booking page and run a test booking yourself. If any of these three fail, nothing else in the plan works.
2. **Build your first prospect list of 150 names.** Search LinkedIn for MDs, owners and managing directors in groundworks, civils, drainage, earthworks and allied trades within 40 miles of Leeds and Sheffield. Filter for businesses with 11 to 50 employees. Save the list. You are looking for the Steve profile: 10 to 20 years in business, owner-operator, Yorkshire-based. Aim for 150 names ready before you send a single message.
3. **Send your first 20 connection requests today.** Use the message already written in your voice section: the one that opens with what you do for MDs in the trade and closes with 'Happy to chat if you are.' Do not change the copy. Do not add a list of services. Send to the 20 best-fit names on your list. Check replies tomorrow morning and handle each one the same day it arrives.

> **Your most likely constraint: conversations that go quiet:** Pam's specialism and credibility will get connections accepted. The drop-off risk is in the follow-up: MDs in construction are busy and slow to respond, and a single message that gets no reply is easy to leave. The fix is a simple two-step follow-up sequence sent five to seven days apart, plain and short, no flannel. Spot the problem early: if accepted connections are climbing but booked calls are not, the follow-up is stalling. Check your reply rate every Friday. If fewer than one in five accepted connections turns into a conversation by week four, the follow-up message needs rewriting before you send another hundred.
